      "content": "Kithure Kindiki Flies to Ethiopia Day After Ruto Returned from Zimbabwe - Tuko.co.ke Most Visited News Website in Kenya 22/24 Kenya Nairobi County Mombasa County Kisumu County Nakuru County Uasin Gishu County Kakamega County Bungoma County Homa Bay County Migori County Trans Nzoia County Kenya Nairobi County Mombasa County Kisumu County Nakuru County Uasin Gishu County Kakamega County Bungoma County Homa Bay County Migori County Trans Nzoia County Global site navigation Business and Economy Technology Economy Industry Money Energy Capital Market Editorial Opinion Feature Analysis Explainer Fact check Entertainment Celebrities TV Shows Movies Music World Africa US Europe Asia Facts and lifehacks Celebrity biographies Guides Stories Fashion and style People Family Relationships Confessions Sports Football Athletics Boxing Kenya Counties Politics Education Local editions Kenya News Habari za Kenya Swahili Home Kenya Kenya Kithure Kindiki Flies to Ethiopia Day After Ruto Returned from Zimbabwe Published 24 Oct 2026 at 11:54 AM by Kai Eli 3 min read Deputy President Kithure Kindiki landed in Bahir Dar aboard a Kenya Air Force aircraft for a continental security forum Ethiopian Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed received Kindiki and the two held a bilateral meeting before the forum opened This year's Tana Forum centres on economic sovereignty and geopolitical transformation as pathways to peace in Africa Search option is now available at TUKO! Feel free to search the content on topics/people you enjoy reading about in the top right corner ;) Deputy President Kithure Kindiki travelled to Ethiopia on Saturday, October 24, touching down at Bahir Dar Dejazmach Belay Zeleke International Airport on board a Kenya Air Force Fokker 70 aircraft. Deputy President Kithure Kindiki boards a plane to Ethiopia. Photo: Kithure Kindiki. Source: Twitter Ethiopian Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed was at hand to receive him. The two leaders would later h\\old a brief bilateral meeting before the main proceedings got under way. \"I was pleased to receive Kenya's Deputy President, Kithure Kindiki, ahead of the 12th Tana High-Level Forum on Security in Africa, where we held a brief bilateral meeting on matters of mutual interest,\" Abiy said, though he did not disclose what specific issues were on the table. Read also James Mugoya Isabirye: Ugandan contractor behind Nairobi's Times Tower, NSSF building Search option is now available at TUKO! Feel free to search the content on topics/people you enjoy reading about in the top right corner ;) Kenya and Ethiopia share a border and are close partners in the Horn of Africa, with security and regional cooperation featuring regularly in their engagements. Kindiki is attending the 12th Tana High-Level Forum on Security in Africa, running from October 23 to 25 in Bahir Dar. The event is organised by the Tana Forum Secretariat and the Institute for Peace and Security Studies at Addis Ababa University. Ghana's President John Mahama, who chairs the Tana Forum Board, is also in attendance. Former presidents Uhuru Kenyatta (Kenya), Goodluck Jonathan (Nigeria), Joyce Banda (Malawi), and Catherine Samba-Panza (the Central African Republic) all sit on the board alongside Mahama. This edition of the forum is built around the theme \"Pathways to Peace in Africa: Economic Sovereignty and Geopolitical Transformation.\" Discussions will explore how Africa can convert its natural resources and digital strengths into broad-based industrial growth, how economic sovereignty can underpin lasting peace, and how to tackle illicit economies that erode governance across the continent. Read also Nairobi to host employability summit to tackle youth unemployment and skills gaps Side events on the forum's margins cover trade and peace, international humanitarian law, climate change and security, and illicit financial flows tied to the conflicts in Sudan and South Sudan. The forum was established in 2012, following the African Union's 2009 Tripoli Declaration, which called for African-led approaches to continental peace and security. Its organisers describe the gathering as modelled on discussions held beneath the baobab tree, combining academic research with practical, on-the-ground experience to produce policy-relevant outcomes. Kindiki's departure came just one day after President William Ruto touched down in Nairobi following his own trip to Harare, where he attended the 25th Comesa Summit of Heads of State and Government. At that meeting, Ruto handed over the chairmanship of the 21-member trading bloc to Zimbabwe's President Emmerson Mnangagwa. The Harare summit also saw the launch of the Comesa Medium-Term Strategic Plan for 2026 to 2030, with deliberations covering intra-African trade, economic integration, artificial intelligence, and broader regional priorities. Source: TUKO.co.ke Authors: Kai Eli (Politics and current affairs editor) Eli Kai is currently working with TUKO as a politics and current affairs editor. He has six years of experience in digital journalism. Eli joined Tuko.co.ke in 2021. Email: eli.odaga@tuko.co.ke Tags: Kithure Kindiki William Ruto Hot: Caroline Lijnen Sheryl Gabriella Female demon names Rick Ness Blonde actresses in their 20s Latest Irungu Kang'ata explains why he abandoned Linda Mwananchi for DCP: \"Hiyo ni AFC Leopards\" Politics 43 minutes ago Oburu Oginga, Sudi, Duale named Kenya's least influential politicians in Research 8020 poll Politics 48 minutes ago Heartbreak as US-based Kenyan man dies at his Texas home, family seeks help US an hour ago NTSA issues statement on what caused Mtito Andei accident that left 22 dead Kenya an hour ago Cléa Menier: French rugby player dies after suffering severe injury during match Sports an hour ago Trending Kenya Met forecasts heavy rains and thunderstorms across several counties until October 13 Kenya 14 days ago Bank employee charged with hacking system, duplicating 2 banking profiles in suspected theft plot Kenya a day ago Kenya Met explains why much-hyped El Niño rains have delayed Kenya 3 days ago Top stories Vybz Kartel opens up about forgiving ex-wife after she cheated on him while in prison Celebrities 6 hours ago Breaking Kenneth Aluma: MP Peter Kaluma's brother dies while undergoing treatment Counties 6 hours ago Diblo Kaberia: Late commentator’s daughter pens emotional tribute 5 months after his death Celebrities 10 hours ago Babu Owino shares approval documents for collapsed Eastleigh building, claims KSh 120m bribe changed hands Counties 3 hours ago Beatrice Murugi: Former marathoner discharged from hospital after long battle with strange illness Athletics 9 hours ago More about our company About Us Our Authors Our Experts Contact Us Media Mentions Our Manifesto Advertise with us Work for us DMCA removal Privacy policy Terms and conditions Policies and standards Cookie policy Tags Categories Do Not Sell My Personal Information Notice at collection Social media Facebook Facebook (Swahili) Instagram YouTube X Telegram TikTok LinkedIn Pinterest Mastodon WhatsApp WhatsApp (Sports) Read us Our applications for phones Our brands Legit.ng Briefly News Yen.com.gh TUKO.co.ke Swahili News TUKO MEDIA LTD, 2026 All rights reserved",
      "summary": "Deputy President Kithure Kindiki traveled to Ethiopia on October 24, 2026, just a day after President William Ruto returned from Zimbabwe. Kindiki arrived in Bahir Dar aboard a Kenya Air Force aircraft to attend the 12th Tana High-Level Forum on Security in Africa, which focuses on economic sovereignty and geopolitical transformation as pathways to peace. Upon arrival, he was welcomed by Ethiopian Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed, and the two leaders held a brief bilateral meeting. The forum, running from October 23 to 25, aims to address how Africa can leverage its natural resources for industrial growth and tackle issues like illicit economies that undermine governance. Notable attendees include Ghana's President John Mahama and former African leaders. This gathering is part of a broader initiative established in 2012 to promote African-led solutions to peace and security challenges. Kindiki's trip underscores the close partnership between Kenya and Ethiopia in regional security matters.",
      "page_url": "https://aynnews.net/news/boss-in-deputy-out-kindiki-flies-out-of-country-after-ruto-s-1e746fc2eb.html"
    }
