    {
      "title": "Turkish Envoy Alkan Meets Police Chief as Ankara Expands Security Footprint - FTL Somalia",
      "link": "https://www.ftlsomalia.com/turkish-envoy-alkan-meets-police-chief-as-ankara-expands-security-footprint/",
      "date": "Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:18:16 GMT",
      "image": "https://ftlsomalia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Turkish-Ambassador-Somali-Police.jpg",
      "content": "Turkish Envoy Alkan Meets Police Chief as Ankara Expands Security Footprint - Somali News today Live Home Politics Security Elections More News Premium Economy & Business Education Entertainment & Lifestyle Environment & Climate Health International Relations Technology & Innovation Sports News By Region Nationwide Benadir Galmudug Hirshabelle Jubaland Puntland South West State Somaliland North Eastern State Resources Infographics Downloads Videos FAQ About Somalia Generic selectors Exact matches only Search in title Search in content Post Type Selectors Home Politics Security Elections More News Premium Economy & Business Education Entertainment & Lifestyle Environment & Climate Health International Relations Technology & Innovation Sports News By Region Nationwide Benadir Galmudug Hirshabelle Jubaland Puntland South West State Somaliland North Eastern State Resources Infographics Downloads Videos FAQ About Somalia Generic selectors Exact matches only Search in title Search in content Post Type Selectors Generic selectors Exact matches only Search in title Search in content Post Type Selectors Security Nationwide Turkish Envoy Alkan Meets Police Chief as Ankara Expands Security Footprint October 25, 2026 4 min read MOGADISHU , A high-level Turkish delegation led by Ambassador Ferhat Alkan visited the headquarters of the Somali Police Force on Sunday, meeting with Police Commissioner Brigadier General Asad Osman Abdullahi to reaffirm Ankara’s commitment to training and equipping Somalia’s elite Haramcad special police unit. According to a statement from the Turkish Embassy in Mogadishu, Ambassador Alkan was accompanied by Murat Daş, a Consultant Special Operations Security Director, and Commissioner Emre Dikyol, a Police Liaison Officer from the Foreign Relations Department of the Turkish General Directorate of Security, along with members of the Turkish Police Special Operations. The embassy described Turkey’s Police Special Operations Directorate as “one of Turkey’s most elite units” and confirmed that its training activities aimed at strengthening the Haramcad Special Police Forces continue “uninterrupted.” The statement also noted that Turkey’s Ministry of Interior, General Directorate of Security, Gendarmerie General Command, and Coast Guard Command are all continuing security cooperation projects with Somalia. This is not a new relationship. As reported in FTL Somalia’s coverage of the police partnership , the Somali Police Chief met with a Turkish delegation in May 2026 to discuss expanding training programs specifically for the Haramcad unit, which has received extensive Turkish support through training, equipment, and modernization. The Haramcad commandos have graduated from the TURKSOM Military Academy in Mogadishu, where they were trained in high-risk operational tactics, rapid response, and civilian protection, as detailed in FTL Somalia’s coverage of the graduation ceremonies . The Turkish Ambassador at the time, Alper Aktaş, stated in August 2026 that Turkey had trained more than 1,000 specialized personnel within the Somali Police Force, in addition to the Gorgor special forces. A Broader Diplomatic Tour Ambassador Alkan’s presence at the police headquarters is consistent with the pattern he has established since presenting his credentials to President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud in late September. He has met with Prime Minister Hamza Abdi Barre to discuss energy, infrastructure, fisheries, security, health, education, space, and connectivity, as reported in FTL Somalia’s coverage of the talks with the Prime Minister . He has visited the spaceport under construction in Warsheikh. He has engaged with the Ministry of Information and met with Somali youth at a Mogadishu café founded by former students in Turkey. The police visit, however, carries particular weight. The Haramcad unit is not a conventional police force. It is a specialized commando unit that has been at the center of Turkey’s security assistance to Somalia, alongside the Gorgor military commandos. Turkey’s investment in these units reflects a broader strategy of building elite, Turkish-trained forces that can operate alongside or independently of the larger, less cohesive Somali National Army. Critical Note The Turkish Embassy’s statement is nothing out of the ordinary, but the presence of a “Consultant Special Operations Security Director” and a police liaison officer from Ankara’s General Directorate of Security, rather than a military attaché, underscores that this is a police-to-police relationship, distinct from Turkey’s military training mission at TURKSOM. The emphasis on “uninterrupted training activities” is also significant. In a security environment where international partners frequently suspend or condition their support based on political developments, Turkey’s commitment to the Haramcad unit has been consistent. That consistency has made Ankara an indispensable partner for the Somali Police Force, but it has also given Turkey a degree of influence over a unit that operates in Somalia’s most sensitive security spaces. For Somalia, the Haramcad model offers a template for building capable, professional forces. But the unit’s effectiveness ultimately depends on its integration into a broader security architecture that includes the police, the military, and the justice system. A well-trained commando unit operating without accountability mechanisms or a functioning criminal justice system is a tool that can protect civilians or intimidate them, depending on who is giving the orders. The Turkish Embassy’s statement thanks the Somali Police Force for its hospitality. The more important question is whether the partnership it describes is building a police force that serves the public, or one that serves the government of the day. Recommended Reading On ftlsomalia.com Somali Police Chief Discusses Security Cooperation with Turkish Delegation Police Chief Graduates Haramcad Commandos at TURKSOM Academy Turkish Ambassador Continues Diplomatic Tour: Discuss with PM Hamza Energy, Security and Space Facebook X Email WhatsApp LinkedIn Somalia’s Danab Commandos Launch Operation Banooda, Kill Seven Al-Shabaab Militants You may also like Security Somalia’s Danab Commandos Launch Operation Banooda, Kill Seven Al-Shabaab Militants October 25, 2026 6 min read Security Min. Fiqi Thanks EU Amb. Máthé for Security Support as Mogadishu Pushes for Faster International Cooperation October 24, 2026 5 min read Security Deadly Oromo-Somali Clashes in Moyale Kill Nine, Displace Thousands to Kenya October 24, 2026 5 min read Latest News Turkish Envoy Alkan Meets Police Chief as Ankara Expands Security Footprint BECO, Mogadishu Power and Blue Sky Announce Rate Increase Amid 70% Fuel Spike Turkish Space Agency Delegation Visits Mogadishu and Warsheikh as Defence Cooperation Expands Puntland’s Deni Rejects Federal Election Process Somali U-17 Squad Celebrated at Parliament as Calls for Sports Investment Grow Hirshabelle Victory Celebrated in Mogadishu as Political Consensus Remains Elusive Oman’s Embassy Reopens in Mogadishu as Al-Umairi Presents Credentials Abiy Ahmed Calls Sea Access an Existential Issue for Ethiopia’s 130 Million People Somalia’s Danab Commandos Launch Operation Banooda, Kill Seven Al-Shabaab Militants Federal and Regional Leaders Congratulate Guudlaawe on Hirshabelle Re-election Facility for Talo and Leadership. Copyright © 2026. All Rights Reserved. ABOUT US | PRIVACY POLICY Home Politics Security Elections More News Premium Economy & Business Education Entertainment & Lifestyle Environment & Climate Health International Relations Technology & Innovation Sports News By Region Nationwide Benadir Galmudug Hirshabelle Jubaland Puntland South West State Somaliland North Eastern State Resources Infographics Downloads Videos FAQ About Somalia",
      "summary": "Turkish Ambassador Ferhat Alkan recently met with Somali Police Commissioner Brigadier General Asad Osman Abdullahi to reinforce Turkey's commitment to training Somalia's elite Haramcad special police unit. This meeting, part of a high-level Turkish delegation's visit to the Somali Police Force headquarters, emphasized ongoing security cooperation between Turkey and Somalia. The Turkish Embassy highlighted that training activities for the Haramcad unit, which specializes in high-risk operations, are continuing without interruption. Turkey has previously trained over 1,000 personnel within the Somali Police Force, reflecting a broader strategy to develop elite forces capable of operating independently of the Somali National Army. Ambassador Alkan's visit aligns with his diplomatic efforts since taking office, including discussions on various sectors such as energy and health. However, the effectiveness of the Haramcad unit hinges on its integration within a comprehensive security framework, raising concerns about accountability and the potential for misuse of power.",
      "page_url": "https://aynnews.net/news/turkish-envoy-alkan-meets-police-chief-as-ankara-expands-sec-b9f37e37eb.html"
